@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki Product To OSB Integration
	Testing Koroneiki Product Integration to osb functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the external links for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| 1234 |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product        |
	| A Liferay Portal Product     |
	| A New Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A New Liferay Portal Product |

Scenario: Create and view product
	Koroneiki products created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |

Scenario: Create and view multiple products
	Multiple products created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name      |
	And I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |

Scenario: Update and view product
	Koroneiki products updated via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name         |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"

Scenario: Update and view multiple products
	Multiple products updated via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A New Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A New Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A New Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A New Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name          |
	And I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A New Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                  | A New Liferay Portal Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key | Verify from name             |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"

Scenario: Remove product and view
	Koroneiki products removed via API should not be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"

Scenario: Remove multiple products and view
	Multiple products removed via API should not be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I should not be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay Portal Product"

Scenario: Create and view product external link
	Koroneiki product external links created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I create a nested field for the product external link with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                      | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key     | Verify from name      |
	| External Link Domain      | liferaydxp            |
	| External Link Entity Id   | 1234                  |
	| External Link Entity Name | LiferayDXP            |

Scenario: Create and view product external link with mapped URL
	Koroneiki product external links with mapped URLs created via API should be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | Koroneiki |
	| Entity Id   | 1234      |
	| Entity Name | Generic   |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should be able to view a product on the sandbox with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name                      | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Koroneiki Product Key     | Verify from name      |
	| External Link Domain      | Koroneiki             |
	| External Link Entity Id   | 1234                  |
	| External Link Entity Name | Generic               |

Scenario: Remove product external link and view
	Koroneiki product external links removed via API should not be viewable on OSB.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Liferay DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "A Liferay DXP Product"
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	Then I should not be able to view a product "A Liferay DXP Product" external link on the sandbox with the domain "liferaydxp" and entity name "LiferayDXP" and entity id "1234"